{"compatibility":"as-is","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: as-is.

Protected data: none.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

No changes were required. The Stan program has no model block likelihood and no parameter priors to check; all top-level data variables (`N`, `alpha`, and `sigma`) are context inputs used only to generate simulated quantities.
","model_safe_stan":"functions {
  // Inverse survival function
  real inv_survival(real u, real alpha, real sigma) {
    return sigma * pow(-log(u), 1 / alpha);
  }
}

data {
  int<lower=1> N;
  real<lower=0> alpha;
  real<lower=0> sigma;
}

generated quantities {
  array[N] real<lower=0> obs_times;

  for (n in 1:N) {
    real u = uniform_rng(0, 1);
    obs_times[n] = inv_survival(u, alpha, sigma);
  }
}
","data_safe_json":"{
  "N": 3,
  "alpha": 2.893169252437498,
  "sigma": 2.0216366472230067
}","protected_variables":[]}
